==========================================
DAY 12 NOTES — Shell Scripting Basics
Date: 12-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- Every bash script starts with #!/bin/bash (the shebang line)
- Variables: NO spaces around = when assigning (name="raven", not name = "raven")
- Use $ to ACCESS a variable's value (echo "$name")
- read -p "prompt: " variable_name lets a script ask for user input
- if [ condition ]; then ... else ... fi is the basic decision structure
- MUST have spaces inside [ ] — [ "$x" = "y" ] works, ["$x"="y"] does NOT
- Scripts need chmod +x before you can run them with ./scriptname.sh
- -f checks if a file exists, -d checks if a directory exists

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] writing a script with a shebang + variable
[ ] chmod +x / ./scriptname.sh
[ ] read -p for user input
[ ] if/else with string and number comparisons
[ ] -f file existence check

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ chmod +x greet.sh && ./greet.sh
> 

$ ./check.sh (with if/else number comparison)
> 


